  "analysis": "yt-dlp is blocked by YouTube's 'Sign in to confirm you're not a bot' bot-detection. yt-dlp also warns it has no JavaScript runtime (only deno enabled by default), and is using a deprecated extraction path. YouTube now requires a JS runtime for proper player extraction, and lacking one may trigger (or fail to bypass) the bot check. Network and apt both work; writes to /app succeed despite df reporting 0 avail. Next step: install a JS runtime (nodejs) so yt-dlp can do proper extraction, then retry with the web client.",
  "plan": "1) Install nodejs via apt (provides the JS runtime yt-dlp needs). 2) Retry yt-dlp format listing using --js-runtimes node and the web player client, which is the most browser-like client and most likely to bypass the bot check. Reading the result tells me whether I can proceed to download.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y nodejs 2>&1 | tail -5\n",
      "duration": 40
    }
  ]
}

